If you have Mac OS X you can build GNU Go using Apple's compiler, which
is derived from GCC. You will need Xcode.

   One issue is that the check for socket support is too
conservative. On OS/X, the check fails, but actually socket
support exists. To connect to the engine through tcp/ip (using gtp)
you may enable the ENABLE_SOCKET_SUPPORT define in config.h.cmake
before configuring. There will be an error message but you may build
the engine and socket support should work.
